# libsqlite3-0: FTS5 and session-extension heap overflows, Debian status
# "affected", no fix shipped. This image's Python is never invoked - the CMP
# runs `sh -c "find . -name '*.enc.yaml' -exec sops -d {} \;"` and sops is a
# static Go binary that does not link SQLite. Checked: no shipped code
# imports sqlite3.
CVE-2026-119373
CVE-2026-119374
CVE-2026-119379

# sops v3.13.3's compiled-in Go dependencies. v3.13.3 is the latest sops
# release (checked against the live GitHub releases API), so there is no
# release to move to - every fix below exists in a newer module or Go
# version that no sops release ships yet. sops runs here for exactly one
# thing: `sops -d` on this repository's own age-encrypted files, with the
# age key mounted locally. In that mode it opens no network connection,
# runs no HTTP/2 or TLS server, serves no files, parses no HTML, JWKs or
# Nickname-profile strings, and verifies no x509 chains - which is where
# every finding below lives:
#   older batch (stdlib, x/crypto, grpc server-side): confirmed by a real
#     scan before M3, same reasoning
#   CVE-2026-111943  crypto/x509 intermediate denylist (outbound TLS MITM)
#   CVE-2026-116587  go-jose DoS via crafted RSA JWKs (cloud-KMS auth path)
#   CVE-2026-56851   x/text Nickname profile panic
#   CVE-2026-78661   x/net/html quadratic parsing
#   CVE-2026-78667   net/http Range-header CPU exhaustion (FileServer/ServeContent)
#   CVE-2026-78669   HTTP/2 SETTINGS-frame CPU exhaustion
#   CVE-2026-97031   crypto/tls ECH memory exhaustion (TLS *server*)
